  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Streaming the Formula 1 Rivalry (2024), published by Peter Lang Verlag, has been cited 9 times. Beyond that, it is used in teaching.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Streaming the Formula 1 Rivalry by Raymond Boyle and Richard Haynes was published by Peter Lang Verlag in 2024. It is part of the Communication, Sport, and Society series. Conceptually, the work connects to Rivalry, Computer science, Economics and Microeconomics.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 9 citations. Citations peaked in 2026 with 5 citing works. Notable citing venues include Media Culture & Society, Leisure Studies and Convergence The International Journal of Research into New Media Technologies. The citing works include 8 journal articles and 1 book chapter. They come from 9 countries, led by the United Kingdom, Australia and Italy.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 1 recorded lecture.</p>",
  "events": {},
